        <briefdescription>
<para>Takes ownership of a pqxx connection and validates it. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Runs <computeroutput>SELECT 1</computeroutput> in a nontransaction when the pointer is non-null and caches <computeroutput>connection_string()</computeroutput> for later use by <ref refid="classDatabase_1a0ec8decb4af7abab6348d85d31f6af70" kindref="member">reconnect()</ref>. A validation failure is logged as critical but does not throw; the object still exists. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="inout">conn</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Connection to take ownership of (moved from the caller).</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
Takes ownership of a connection, validates it and caches its connection string. A failed validation is logged (critical) but does not throw; the object still exists with the supplied pointer. <ref refid="classDatabase_1a0ec8decb4af7abab6348d85d31f6af70" kindref="member">reconnect()</ref> later depends on the cached string. conn: Connection moved into this <ref refid="classDatabase" kindref="compound">Database</ref>. </para>
