      <memberdef kind="function" id="classDatabase_1a7c0a44631de74f1d0a18119d1cd6cf1a" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>bool</type>
        <definition>bool Database::checkExists</definition>
        <argsstring>(const std::string &amp;table, const std::string &amp;column, const std::string &amp;value)</argsstring>
        <name>checkExists</name>
        <qualifiedname>Database::checkExists</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const std::string &amp;</type>
          <declname>table</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const std::string &amp;</type>
          <declname>column</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const std::string &amp;</type>
          <declname>value</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Returns whether a row exists in a table for the given column value. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Builds <computeroutput>SELECT EXISTS (...)</computeroutput> using <computeroutput>quote_name</computeroutput> for the table and column to prevent SQL injection, binding only the value as a parameter. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">table</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Table name (identifier, quoted). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">column</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Column name (identifier, quoted). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">value</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Value bound to the <computeroutput>$1</computeroutput> placeholder. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><computeroutput>true</computeroutput> if the row exists; <computeroutput>false</computeroutput> if it does not or if the query threw. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>A query error is indistinguishable from &quot;not found&quot; here (both return <computeroutput>false</computeroutput>); use <ref refid="classDatabase_1a5941bc7b94fbacc46dd8acc818712afd" kindref="member">check_connection()</ref> when that distinction matters.</para>
</simplesect>
Checks whether a row exists using a parameterised EXISTS query. Table and column are passed through <computeroutput>quote_name</computeroutput> (identifiers cannot be bound as parameters); only the value is bound. The transaction scope is closed before the result is read so no idle transaction is left open on the connection. table: Table name. column: Column name. value: Value bound to <computeroutput>$1</computeroutput>. Returns <computeroutput>true</computeroutput> if the row exists; <computeroutput>false</computeroutput> if not, or if the query threw. Note: Query failures are swallowed and reported as <computeroutput>false</computeroutput> (see the header note). </para>
        </detaileddescription>
