        <name>reconnect</name>
        <qualifiedname>Database::reconnect</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Replaces the wrapped connection with a fresh one built from the cached string. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Rebuilds the wrapped connection from the string cached at construction.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>The result of <ref refid="classDatabase_1a5941bc7b94fbacc46dd8acc818712afd" kindref="member">check_connection()</ref> on the new connection; <computeroutput>false</computeroutput> on failure. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Not thread-safe: callers must ensure no query is in flight. The old connection is released when the <computeroutput>shared_ptr</computeroutput> is replaced.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The health check result of the new connection; <computeroutput>false</computeroutput> if creation or check failed.</para>
</simplesect>
The old connection is dropped when the <computeroutput>shared_ptr</computeroutput> is reassigned. The failure path is logged as critical. Not thread-safe: the caller must own the <ref refid="classDatabase" kindref="compound">Database</ref> exclusively (see <ref refid="classDatabaseConnectionPool_1a51134b38454f5146921c081fbf2ad5f3" kindref="member">DatabaseConnectionPool::reconnect_all</ref> and the watchdog). <simplesect kind="pre"><para><ref refid="classDatabase_1a5941bc7b94fbacc46dd8acc818712afd" kindref="member">check_connection()</ref> returned false, or a reconnect was otherwise requested. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
