Executes a parameterised query and converts result rows to JSON. Commits the transaction only when TransactionType is <computeroutput>pqxx::work</computeroutput>; a <computeroutput>pqxx::nontransaction</computeroutput> simply ends at scope exit. Columns are converted by PostgreSQL type OID, with unhandled types falling back to a string. Template parameter jsonType: <computeroutput>jsoncons::json</computeroutput> (returns the first row) or <computeroutput>jsoncons::json::array</computeroutput> (returns all rows); any other type is rejected by a static_assert. Template parameter TransactionType: Transaction wrapper used for the execution. query: SQL text with <computeroutput>$1, $2, ...</computeroutput> placeholders. params: Values bound to those placeholders. Returns The converted value, or <computeroutput>std::nullopt</computeroutput> if any exception was caught. Note: For the single-object specialisation an empty result yields a default-constructed JSON value, not <computeroutput>std::nullopt</computeroutput> (only exceptions produce <computeroutput>std::nullopt</computeroutput>). </para>
