    <briefdescription>
<para>Owns one synchronous PostgreSQL connection used by the synchronous database path. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>A <ref refid="classDatabase" kindref="compound">Database</ref> wraps a single <computeroutput>pqxx::connection</computeroutput> and offers the query helpers used by controllers through a <ref refid="classDatabaseHanndler" kindref="compound">DatabaseHanndler</ref> lease. Instances are constructed and owned by <ref refid="classDatabaseConnectionPool" kindref="compound">DatabaseConnectionPool</ref>, which hands them out one borrower at a time; callers never construct one directly. The constructor validates the connection with <computeroutput>SELECT 1</computeroutput> and caches its connection string so <ref refid="classDatabase_1a0ec8decb4af7abab6348d85d31f6af70" kindref="member">reconnect()</ref> can rebuild it later. <verbatim>     Thread-safety: the wrapped connection is used by one borrower at a
</verbatim> time as enforced by the pool, so no internal locking is performed. Non-copyable and non-movable: ownership stays with the pool&apos;s <computeroutput>std::shared_ptr</computeroutput>. <simplesect kind="note"><para>The constructor tolerates a null connection (no validation performed and an empty cached connection string); in normal operation the pool passes a validated connection. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classDatabaseConnectionPool" kindref="compound">DatabaseConnectionPool</ref>, <ref refid="classDatabaseHanndler" kindref="compound">DatabaseHanndler</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
